  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">EU partnership for sustainable energy practices in industry</narrative>
  </title>
  <description type="1">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">The four-year Switch Garment project in Cambodia, which was funded by the EU and carried out by UNIDO, Geres, and TAFATC, aimed at integrating sustainable energy initiatives into the GFT sector&apos;s energy profile. The project came to an end in May 2024. The proposed present project, to take place between 25.06.2026 - 27.05.2028, will support transition of the GFT sector through conducting energy audits, providing capacity building programs and developing financing schemes to ensure better access to finance. To build on the earlier project achievements, the EU approved a follow-up bilateral project #EU Partnership for Sustainable Energy Practices in Industry#. In addition to maintaining the momentum created by EU-Switch Garment, this project takes into account the recent advancements in Cambodia&apos;s sustainable energy and efficiency aspect, the Power Development Plan (PDP), and new initiatives on renewable energy including sustainable biomass and roof top solar installations.</narrative>
  </description>
